{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470966-superiors-and-super-soldier-serums-in-history","id":1470966,"title":"Superiors and Super Soldier Serums in history","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-20T15:46:22-08:00","id":1470966,"title":"Superiors and Super Soldier Serums in history","content":"I really like the idea of Superiors and I think the idea of using the result of most &quot;Super Soldier Serums&quot; as resulting in giving the recipient of the &quot;Serum&quot; (or whatever was used to cause the change, but Serum for simplicities sake) the Superior Template makes a lot of sense in the Trinity Continuum setting. Like, the easiest way to force someone into expressing enhanced ability is to make them a Superior. So I like to think that the process of making a Superior was discovered multiple different times throughout history. In fact, the process for making a Superior might be drastically different depending on who developed the process.<br /> <br /> So what are some good ideas for different ways someone might have made a Superior? I, personally, like the idea of using something like the flower the king's used in Wakanda. Maybe some ancient African kingdom has legends of being ruled by warrior and philosopher kings that some modern faction discovers is based in truth. You can also use the classic Captain America scenario, that's a good one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T15:51:47-08:00","id":1470967,"title":"","content":"A nova that's styling himself as the emperor of mankind is building a space empire and decides he needs some space marines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T18:26:13-08:00","id":1470973,"title":"","content":"Adventure! lists super soldier programs as a potential origin/Inspiration for Stalwarts. Perhaps some could be misidentify or confuse the two 'templates', so maybe some of those could have been Superiors.<br /> Interestingly, the Transcendent Alliance would definitely gather and attempt to recreate as many of these as possible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T18:39:38-08:00","id":1470975,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Stalwarts might be something I might use for this idea too, but I got the rules for Superior's right now. I'm interested to see if there is any overlap. I'm guessing probably not that much.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what my headcanon for &quot;Super Soldiers&quot; from history will be when I get access to the Adventure! book. Depends on what Stalwarts feel like, I guess. I do like how &quot;artificial&quot; the Superior Template feels. It's distinct from more naturally occurring Inspired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T02:40:46-08:00","id":1470990,"title":"","content":"Super-soldier serums are indeed a good idea for &quot;Adventure!&quot;. If I were to include something like that in my campaign, however, I would add heavy side effects to the corresponding serums - even if these were only present narratively. On the one hand, the superiors would still feel like technological progress and on the other hand, this would fit perfectly story-wise. Moreover, super serums with nasty side effects make for more interesting stories than super serums without nasty side effects.<br /> <br /> The miracle flower of the African philosopher king? Gives you superpowers. If you survive eating it, because it kills 99 out of 100 warriors who try it.<br /> <br /> Dr. Klaus-G\u00fcnther Kurpfuscher's super serum extracted from gorilla pineal glands? Gives you superpowers. Makes you as dumb as toast.<br /> <br /> The ancient Chinese &quot;spirit potion&quot; kept closely guarded in a remote monastery? Gives you superpowers. And psychotic episodes where you think you're the mythological demon Ni\u00fa M\u00f3w\u00e1ng.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T03:11:42-08:00","id":1470993,"title":"","content":"In my view there is a huge difference between a Super Soldier Serum and becoming a Superior/Stalwart, but it is mostly due to the nature of power in TC.<br /> <br /> Trasitionaly, a super soldier serum would GIVE powers to the character, in this case the side effects would make sense, as the powers are modifications in the body of the character that are not supposed to happen in any way.<br /> <br /> Superiors have their power RELEASED in a controlled way, in other words, the treatment didn\u2019t give the character any power, it just controlled and induced the character to show their powers, powers that were part of them and were supposed to show up eventually. In this case it\u2019s not the serum that defines the powers, but the nature of the character, and the side effects would not be something related to the treatment too, mostly.<br /> <br /> If the idea is the build a serum, the powers and results of the serum would be previously defined (even if not what the inventor intended), like MCU One, where all are super strong, fast and resistant, and have a big thing for uncontrolled physical violence demonstration.<br /> <br /> Superiors have different Fortes and their powers are everywhere in superhuman capacities, basically like a nova, or Stalwart, but controled in its level of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T12:37:47-08:00","id":1471028,"title":"","content":"Basically, it's possible to use the super science rule to add extraordinary capabilities to ordinary people. Sometimes even superhuman abilities. That said, it can be difficult in practice to tell the difference between an ordinary person who has had superhuman abilities grafted on through super science, and a Superior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T14:44:10-08:00","id":1471035,"title":"","content":"I think a big limitation on most Super Soldier type characters would be severe restrictions on gaining new super abilities. Captain Victorious may gain more dots in whatever powers he already has without difficulty since that is just a matter of training his scientifically granted abilities, but gaining new powers may require another session in the Evolution Chamber, and may even be impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T14:57:07-08:00","id":1471036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470966-superiors-and-super-soldier-serums-in-history?p=1471035#post1471035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a big limitation on most Super Soldier type characters would be severe restrictions on gaining new super abilities. Captain Victorious may gain more dots in whatever powers he already has without difficulty since that is just a matter of training his scientifically granted abilities, but gaining new powers may require another session in the Evolution Chamber, and may even be impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly the point differentiating a supertech that unlock the powers from one that give the powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T15:02:00-08:00","id":1471039,"title":"","content":"To be fair, superior should probably have some restrictions on what new powers they develop over time. Conceptual synergy, if you will. While technically allowed, it's not good for to take a character who has been developing a whole bunch of nimblements type power, and suddenly Grant him something based off of super smarts. But that's not so much a rule restriction as it is a narrative one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T15:27:05-08:00","id":1471041,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Flower of the African Philosopher Kings kills 99 out of 100 people who take it&quot; would definitely be my take on that particular Super Soldier Serum. I might actually go &quot;Resident Evil&quot; with it and have the flower actually holding a kind of virus that is responsible for the empowering process. A virus that just so happens to create zombies when it doesn't create a Superior. Boom. Zombie outbreak story to go with your Super Soldier origin.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm thinking that that most of the created Super Soldier Serums, outside of the historical ones that have various unique properties that keep them from being mass produced, would be Super Prototype style creations that get their plans destroyed and only result in one subject before being destroyed. Of course, there is nothing stopping you from making it so that some new or existing faction just develops working Super Soldier creation techniques. Transcendent Alliance would be an obvious choice. So rather than the Nakamura Process being developed in the Aeon era you might get, say, the Templeton Process developed in the modern day setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}